const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文把买卖价差与资产定价联系起来，讨论交易摩擦可能如何进入预期回报研究。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开描述以价差或流动性摩擦的测量为条件，对资产或组合的回报关系进行比较。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要明确价差来自报价、成交还是代理估计，并保留频率、市场、证券筛选和测量时钟。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"价差可以代表某些交易摩擦，但它不是完整执行成本，也不应被视为所有流动性维度的同义词。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"分开报告报价价差、有效价差、价格冲击和费用，并将异常报价、非交易日和公司行动处理写明。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Economics (2000)。一项流动性代理与回报的历史关联，不构成对任一证券未来回报或成交能力的承诺。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Economics (2000) for “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-405X(99)00067-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。一项流动性代理与回报的历史关联，不构成对任一证券未来回报或成交能力的承诺。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Asset Pricing and the Bid-Ask Spread”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
